                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Proposed Paragraph for Insertion in Note to Germany</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Government of the U. S. nevertheless realizes that a belligerent ought not to
                    be deprived of the use of the submarine in its efforts to interrupt commerce
                    with the enemy provided the operations of the submarine do not jeopardize human
                    life or result in the indiscriminate destruction of neutral property. The Govt.
                    of the U. S. is willing, therefore, to consider any suggestion, which the German
                    Imperial Government may see fit to make, looking toward a modification of the
                    existing rules of international law governing naval warfare applicable to the
                    use of submarines which will efficiently safeguard the lives of persons and
                    neutral property on merchant vessels which are intercepted on the high seas.</p>
            </div>
